  "details": "I created a very large but simple system to control things in my worlds, I wanted to do it for many reasons of my own.\n\nThis graph code ended up like this, \"Address: '512' is larger than the UdonVM's heap size of '512'.\"\n\nAt first I thought it was a bug, so I restarted unity, and when I tried to open the code, while still seeing the problem, I saw the code was no longer loading.\n\nI can't edit it anymore, I can't see what I did anymore, it's a blank page.\n\nI wish I'd at least known what I'd done to translate this into UdonSharp now that I'm aware of such a bad limitation, but now I have to start all over again, as udon can't load the 4000 lines into the .asset file it created.\n\nIt doesn't matter which version of udon you are in.\n\nThank you again",
